Re: Letter in Support of Liquor License Transfer Application
Mayor and Council Members:
This Letter is in support of 307 Horse Racing, Inc.'s Liquor License Transfer Application
with the City of Cheyenne being transferred to it by Stu lts Management Company currently
located at the existing licensed location at1600E.Pershing Ave.and is designed toprovide
supplemental information to the application.
In Mayand June 2021,307Horse Racing, Inc.completed a successful slate of16race days
at the Cam-Plexin Gillette which brought substantial traffic, visitors and income into Campbell
County in support of bringing horse racing back to this wonderful community for thelonghaul.
It is setfor another16days of live racing at the Cam-Plexagainin May-June 2022.As part of these
liverace days307Horse Racing ran more days thanhad ever been run in Gillette and paid out
more purse money than everbefore.Even more purse moneyis available forthe 2022race slate.
307 Horse Racing, Inc.is hopefulto begin running a full live event horse racing slate in Cheyenne
in the near future.
It is now working on openinga gaming parlorin Cheyenne, hopefully in support of that
mission, i.e.to continue to run better and better horse racing slates in Cheyenne, Gillette, and in
gaming parlor located at 1510 E. Pershing Blvd in Cheyenne.It would propose to move the
same commercial retail complex.
307 Horse Racing's Affiliated entity, Wyoming Financial Properties, Inc. owns the
Cheyenne Business Center complex located at 1510 E.Pershingin Cheyenne.The Office Bar&
Eatery(Stults Management Company)has held theliquor license sought to be transferred at this
